<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ayyanadikal Thiruvadikal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Ayyan Adikal Thiruvadikal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ayyanadikal Thiruvadikal was the ruler of Venad in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> in the mid-ninth century, under the overlordship of the Chera Perumal king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sthanu-ravi">Sthanu Ravi</a>. In the Tharisapalli <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> plates of 849 he granted land, serfs and trading privileges to the Syrian Christian church of Tarisa at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kollam">Kollam</a>. The plates are among the earliest dated records of Kerala's history and of its Christian community.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ayyanadikal-thiruvadikal.jpg" alt="Ayyanadikal Thiruvadikal" width="294" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karanmana K. Rajagopal, Rajeswari Menon and Ramani Balasankar (Madhavan Nayar Foundation, Cochin) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayyan_Atikal_gifting_the_Quilon_Syrian_copper_plates_to_Maruvan_Sapir_Iso.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
